  "comparison_notes": [
    "Map records by their typed identity and global row/size; require exact canonical bytes and content SHA for these 15 per-row records, with no missing/extra/duplicate rows.",
    "The fourth transition is the aggregate family_partial_calibration record, not a per-row pseudo_family_plan. Its whole SHA is allowed and expected to change.",
    "Verify the old and new record payload/file hashes and archived references separately. New record must pass its unmodified own reader with current_source_binding=True.",
    "Do NOT overwrite the old record or re-label the new record as engine0.107 or Python3.13.15.",
    "New binding must identify the new fixed module SHA map, rules/tables and registered constants; invariant science/input dependency fields must equal baseline.",
    "Do not require whole gate dict equality: recorded env and registered expected Python differ. Both gates must be independently valid in their own execution epoch; new precheck/prelaunch and twelve gate must be live collected, exact new six versions and BLAS constraints.",
    "Exact numeric per-row comparison is for the fixed first3 only; it excludes unexercised N4/KDE-CI/12-position numerical paths and does not approve screening/certificates/target.",
    "On mismatch preserve artifacts and stop for analysis; distinguish expected metadata differences from any actual numeric/state/identity differences. No retry-until-match or retrospectively chosen tolerance."
  ]
